a rocker takes a stab at shakespearean  horror while two snl alums try to keep a  straight face  from oscar nominees to mcu favorites you  won't believe who's gotten a paycheck  from lifetime  in a 2020 interview with tv insider  sigourney weaver called her role as  fundamentalist mother turned lgbtq plus  advocate mary griffith in the 2009  lifetime movie prayers for bobby the  hardest part she'd ever played from an  emotional standpoint the role of based  on the experiences of the real life  griffith required weaver to take an  unsympathetic turn as a homophobic  mother who tried to convert her son  played by ryan kelly after he came out  as gay after his suicide she rejects her  bigoted views and becomes a powerful  voice in support of gay rights if i just  listen to my son when he poured his  heart out to me  i would not be standing here today  weaver earned emmy golden globe and  screen actors guild nominations for her  performance as griffith who came to  believe that her church's interpretation  of scripture was wrong and worked  tirelessly until the end of her life for  pro-gay causes reversals of faith and  demoral searches are no small feats to  depict on screen but weaver's  performance taps directly into  griffith's anguish over losing her son  to find both healing and renewed purpose  depicting griffith as a heartless figure  wouldn't have made her newfound beliefs  and direction so moving or being  accurate to the real-life griffith  weaver instead does a heavy lifting to  find the humanity and humility in  griffith which lends extraordinary depth  to her performance  made us a point in christian stuart's  career when she was just emerging from  juvenile roles and long before her vote  to stardom in the twilight saga and the  string of critically praised adult  performances the 2004 lifetime drama  speak confirms her exceptional acting  talent stewards plays a high schooler  who has difficulty talking after being  sexually assaulted at a house party  speak which premiered at the sundance  film festival in 2004 before airing on  lifetime and showtime in 2005 is based  on a young adult novel by laurie hulls  anderson both the source material and  the film handle that subject matter with  great sensitivity and emotional depth  speak gets tremendous support from the  uniformly excellent cast which includes  elizabeth perkins and d.b sweeney as  stuart's parents steve zahn is a  sympathetic teacher and michael angerano  as a fellow outcast who befriends stuart  but it's stewart's performance that  anchors the film and elevates it beyond  typical lifetime fare the trials of her  character are a lot for any actor to  carry but stuart shoulders it with  strength and maturity  jason momoa's acting career was still in  its embryonic phase when he signed on to  play a mostly shirtless love interest  for virginia madison in a 2003 lifetime  movie tempted  you know what you need you get in the  water  it's healing  i'm not the best swimmer  i am mamoa completed his first screen  assignment a two season run on baywatch  hawaii shortly before signing until  tempted despite its hawaiian setting  temted was actually filmed in new south  wales australia  maggie greenwald is talented and  award-winning director of such  well-regarded indie dramas as a ballad  of little joe and suncatcher benefits  from the natural beauty of her film's  locations and her cast the film pairs  mamoa with virginia madison as a woman  who travels with the ashes of her former  guardian and native hawaiian there she  meets momoa who plays her late  guardian's nephew and sparks fly despite  the fact that madsen has a husband  waiting for her on the mainland mamoa  who is a naturally charismatic and  intense performer doesn't have much to  do here beyond staring longingly while  wearing as little clothing as possible  if you're a fan of his work in aquaman  dune and sea this isn't an exemplary  showcase for his abilities but if you're  interested in his chiseled build tempted  is a two-hour box of eye candy  though mark ruffalo is one of  hollywood's busiest and most acclaimed  actors today the emmy grammy tony and  oscar nominee was largely anonymous in  the 1990s ruffalo's resume during this  period included low budget horror and  indie films but he also kept busy with  occasional forays into tv like on the  second day of christmas which aired on  lifetime television in 1997 directed by  james frawley on the second day of  christmas takes place in a department  store during the holidays but it's no  miracle on 34th street despite being a  little girl patsy played by lauren pratt  is an experienced pickpocket who works  as a team with her aunt played by mary  stuart masterson ruffalo is a department  store security guard who catches them in  the act so writer brian holfeld bends  logic to force a trio to spend christmas  together while awaiting sentencing  christmas is supposed to be a time of  compassion don't you feel the least bit  sorry for us look lady you choose the  life of crime you got to take the  consequences while many holiday romance  couples seem forced together by the plot  ruffalo and masterson's chemistry helps  to make their eventual connection seem  believable  in 2011 lifetime presented 5 an  anthology feature featuring stories  about the impact of breast cancer on  patients and their families the project  created by marta kaufman drew high  profile talent behind the camera  including jennifer aniston alicia keys  and patty jenkins it also attracted  talented performers like patricia  clarkson tracy ellis russ rosario dawson  and tony shalhoub two years later  lifetime returned to the 5 format for  call me crazy which focused its quintet  of stories on mental health issues 5  gained an emmy award nomination for  casting and numerous nominations for its  actors and directors so when the network  decided to return to the format for  2013's call me crazy a five film they  garnered an even more impressive roster  of talent directors included oscar  winner laura dern bryce dallas howard  ashley judd and bonnie hunt while three  oscar winners jennifer hudson octavia  spencer and melissa leo each headlined  one of the stories  by the age of 20 kiersten dunst had a  massive impressive body of work in films  and on television she earned her first  of four golden globe nominations at the  age of 10 for interview with the vampire  and featured in such popular and  critical hits as little women jumanji  wag the dog and the virgin suicides  during this incredibly busy period the  future oscar and emmy nominee also  starred in a lifetime original movie 15  and pregnant dunce is a titular teenager  tina who becomes pregnant by her  deadbeat boyfriend ray played by daniel  coons she decides to keep the baby  causing friction between her separated  parents played by park overall and david  andrews and her sister played by julia  wellen the film hits all the pregnancy  drama tropes tina's dramatic reveal ray  bailing on being a dad and a birth  sequence filled with screaming but it  also does well in dividing the focus  between tina and her extended family and  friends you're not my leader i don't act  and think like you well it wouldn't be  so terrible for you to be a little less  shallow maybe a little bit more  responsible you're not that great either  you know dunce portrays the confusion of  teen life and the upheaval of an  unexpected pregnancy with the same depth  and confidence she's shown throughout  her career the majority of her scenes  pitter against overall and andrews two  extremely capable stage trained  performers and she holds her own in  every scene  the drama stockholm pennsylvania  surprised many sundance film goers by  premiering on lifetime in 2015 rather  than hitting theaters after garnering  mostly positive reviews at the festival  that year the film features an  impressive cast led by oscar nominee  sergio ronan and emmy winner cynthia  nixon and tackles a difficult subject  the impact of an abduction on both the  victim and her family  ronan plays 22 year old leia who was  held captive from the age of four by a  man with apocalyptic delusions named ben  played by jason isaacs eventually she  returns to her parents played by nixon  and david washowski that she barely  knows what follows is at times an even  more intense take on life after trauma  than is depicted in room with free  lassen leia's refusal to accept her  parents and fund recollections of life  with ben  all signs point to stockholm syndrome  ronin avoids the pitfall of overplaying  a deeply damaged character  she remains quiet instead of explosive  or unhinged allowing the viewer to guess  at her true emotional state  when lifetime steps out of the romantic  thriller of suburban drama box the end  result is often a high-profile project  like call me crazy or betty and coretta  trying something different really meant  casting courtney love dominic monaghan  and paul walter hauser in a horror  themed series based on shakespeare's and  midsummer's night dream of course that's  exactly what lifetime provided with  2017's and midsummer's nightmare  produced in partnership with a e studios  after the success of their hit drama  unreal lifetime appeared to be aiming  for american horror story territory with  a midsummer's nightmare a midsummer's  nightmare opens on a strong note with a  character dragged through the woods by  mass figures that hurl her into an open  grave filled with bees once that initial  shock fades away however the film  becomes a routine mix of tristing and  low wattage mystery  the campus  time to scamper  a deadly adoption is sort of a  meta-lifetime movie it's a parody of the  network's sudsy plotting with will  ferrell and kristen wiig playing the  sort of hapless suburbanites usually  portrayed by the likes of eric roberts  and kelly martin though produced by  farrell's former partner adam mckay a  deadly adoption unfolds with an entirely  straight face requiring the audience to  find the laughs in the inherent  absurdity of the story itself feral and  wig who work hard to achieve a sort of  earnest blindness are robert and sarah a  married couple who lose their second  child in an unfortunate dark accident  they soon decide on using a surrogate to  have another child but their prospective  birth mother bridget played by lifetime  vet jessica lowndes is more than she  seems she's actually obsessed with  robert farrell's trademark near hysteria  and wigs over dramatic referees are put  to good use here but the humor is almost  too subtle there's just a razor thin  margin between the comedy and the  histrionics of a real lifetime movie  [Music]  you

